From 6026b7e5ec7c8e1d63a3e4da1d64977d0b95a989 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:28:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hackberrypi): Waydroid keeps its network and hides its
 full-UI launcher

Waydroid's LXC config mounts cgroup read-only, so Android's init can't
create a process group for each app ("createProcessGroup ... Read-only
file system" for every service). When system_server dies, Android then
can't kill the old app processes. The stale NetworkStack keeps running
and the new one never provisions eth0, which leaves no default route.
On the HackberryPi, killing system_server lost the route every time
with cgroup:ro. With cgroup:rw, Android builds uid_*/pid_* groups under
lxc.payload.waydroid, the stale processes go away, and the route comes
back. Four session restarts in a row all had a route.

Waydroid.desktop only opens Waydroid's full UI, which closes every
per-app window in multi-window mode, so it gets NoDisplay=true. The
Android apps have their own entries.
---
 mkosi.images/base/mkosi.postinst | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mkosi.images/base/mkosi.postinst b/mkosi.images/base/mkosi.postinst
index 36b16a4..896ae3e 100755
--- a/mkosi.images/base/mkosi.postinst
+++ b/mkosi.images/base/mkosi.postinst
@@ -592,3 +592,16 @@ EOF
 
 ln -sf ../marathon-flathub-setup.service \
     "$BUILDROOT/usr/lib/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/marathon-flathub-setup.service"
+
+# Waydroid (HackberryPi image, Deckard M0).
+WAYDROID_LXC="$BUILDROOT/usr/lib/waydroid/data/configs/config_base"
+if [ -f "$WAYDROID_LXC" ]; then
+    # Android kills apps by process group; read-only cgroups leave them running.
+    sed -i 's/^lxc.mount.auto = cgroup:ro /lxc.mount.auto = cgroup:rw /' "$WAYDROID_LXC"
+    grep -q '^lxc.mount.auto = cgroup:rw ' "$WAYDROID_LXC"
+fi
+WAYDROID_DESKTOP="$BUILDROOT/usr/share/applications/Waydroid.desktop"
+if [ -f "$WAYDROID_DESKTOP" ]; then
+    # Full UI closes every per-app window; Android apps have their own entries.
+    sed -i '/^\[Desktop Entry\]$/a NoDisplay=true' "$WAYDROID_DESKTOP"
+fi
-- 
